      "topic": "background",
      "summary": "Warm-season fruiting crop; harvest can be green or fully coloured. Chilling impairs growth and frost damages plants. Excessive day or night heat can reduce flower retention and fruit set. Solanaceous crops may share problems, but broad-host pathogens such as Phytophthora require wider consideration. Harvest colour, cultivar and repeated picking change the full cycle; seedling and field phases should be separated.",
